#usda 1.0
(
    doc = """Imageable fixture (task 1.6): an invisible Xform whose child
    authors visibility = "inherited", which USD still treats as invisible.

    USD visibility prunes. A prim is invisible if it or any Imageable ancestor
    authors "invisible", and a descendant cannot opt back in: "inherited" is
    the schema default and means "whatever my parent is". So
    /Root/Hidden/ChildInherited is invisible in USD although its own attribute
    says "inherited".

    Godot's Node3D.visible prunes the same way, so the importer sets the flag
    on the prim that authors "invisible" and nowhere else, and Godot hides the
    rest.

    Every Mesh is the quad_mesh.usda quad.

    EXPECTED -- to_imageable_data, per prim
      /Root/Hidden                  visible = false   purpose default
      /Root/Hidden/ChildInherited   visible = true    purpose default
      /Root/Sibling                 visible = true    purpose default
      no warnings on any prim

      `visible` is the prim's own flag, not its effective visibility, so
      ChildInherited's true is correct.

    DETECTOR: an importer that also flags the descendants of an invisible prim
    hides the same nodes and looks identical in the viewport. The difference
    shows when Hidden is made visible again in the editor: the subtree stays
    hidden, because each child now carries its own flag. ChildInherited's
    visible = true is the whole assertion."""
    defaultPrim = "Root"
    metersPerUnit = 1
    upAxis = "Y"
)

def Xform "Root"
{
    def Xform "Hidden"
    {
        token visibility = "invisible"

        def Mesh "ChildInherited"
        {
            float3[] extent = [(-1, 0, -1), (1, 0, 1)]
            int[] faceVertexCounts = [4]
            int[] faceVertexIndices = [0, 1, 2, 3]
            point3f[] points = [(-1, 0, -1), (-1, 0, 1), (1, 0, 1), (1, 0, -1)]
            token visibility = "inherited"
        }
    }

    def Mesh "Sibling"
    {
        float3[] extent = [(-1, 0, -1), (1, 0, 1)]
        int[] faceVertexCounts = [4]
        int[] faceVertexIndices = [0, 1, 2, 3]
        point3f[] points = [(-1, 0, -1), (-1, 0, 1), (1, 0, 1), (1, 0, -1)]
    }
}
